          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.21,
            0.884,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "The magnets used by sailors in the olden days were based on naturally occurring magnets, known as lodestones which were discovered in ancient times. Later on, people found out that magnets could also be made from pieces of iron. Nowadays, we have magnets made of different materials. The magnets that you find in your school laboratory and those used in pencil boxes, stickers, toys are all artificial magnets (Fig. 4.1). The magnets can be of various shapes, some of which are shown in Fig. 4.2."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.407,
            0.878,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
